/*
 * Localizable.strings (es) — Spanish (pak0: spanish_*.lang)
 *
 * D-088 slice 1 + D-112 slices 2-3. The comment above each entry says where it
 * came from:
 *   #str_NNNNN        copied from openQ4's own pak0 string table for this
 *                     language (vendor/openQ4/content/baseoq4/pak0/strings/),
 *                     recased from the menu's ALL CAPS, accents restored;
 *   #str_NNNNN + MT   built around that pak0 term, the rest machine-translated;
 *   MT                machine-translated, using the words pak0 uses for the
 *                     same concepts. Not yet read by a native speaker —
 *                     docs/localization-map.md lists what to check first.
 *
 * Every key the shell reads is present (scripts/check-localization.py). The
 * per-key English fallback still exists for any key a later change adds.
 */

